{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b0f04261-98d3-5443-a6e8-cc775426b846",
    "name": "Ch 23 - Insecure Endpoint Findings (fails on purpose)",
    "description": "Chapter 23. Folder 1 runs tests that describe SECURE behavior against the deliberately insecure /api/insecure/* endpoints, so they FAIL ON PURPOSE: each failure is one finding. Folder 2 runs the same expectations against the normal endpoints, and they pass. Expected result: 6 of 13 assertions fail, all in folder 1. Only test systems you own or have written permission to test. A full run takes about 25 seconds (two expired-token checks wait 11 seconds each).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 Insecure endpoints (fail on purpose)",
      "description": "Each test describes the SECURE behavior, so it fails on the deliberately insecure /api/insecure/* endpoints. Each failure is one finding.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Log in as tester",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Login works (200)', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "BOLA: read buyer2's order",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Expected (secure) behavior: another user's order is NOT returned",
                  "pm.test(\"API1 BOLA: tester must not read buyer2's order\", function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'status').to.eql(404);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insecure/orders/1002",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "insecure",
                "orders",
                "1002"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Mass assignment: register as admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('newUser', `qa.mass.${Date.now()}`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Expected: the server sets role itself and ignores the client's \"role\"",
                  "pm.test('API3 Mass assignment: new account must get role user', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().role).to.eql('user');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insecure/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "insecure",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{newUser}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Pass@1234\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in with the new account",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Expected: a self-registered account never gets admin rights",
                  "const role = pm.response.json().user.role;",
                  "console.log('the new account logged in with role:', role);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('API3 Impact: the new account must not be admin', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(role).to.not.eql('admin');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{newUser}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Pass@1234\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Broken token check: expired token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Get a token that lives 10 seconds, then wait 11 seconds",
                  "// (skipped when an expired token is already stored)",
                  "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('shortToken')) {",
                  "  pm.sendRequest({",
                  "    url: pm.variables.replaceIn('{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login'),",
                  "    method: 'POST',",
                  "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
                  "    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({",
                  "      username: pm.variables.get('username'),",
                  "      password: pm.variables.get('password'),",
                  "      expiresIn: 10 }) }",
                  "  }, function (err, res) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('shortToken', res.json().token);",
                  "    setTimeout(function () {}, 11000);",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Expected: an expired token is refused with 401 TOKEN_EXPIRED",
                  "pm.test('API2 Broken auth: expired token must be refused', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'status').to.eql(401);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql('TOKEN_EXPIRED');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.unset('shortToken');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insecure/profile",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "insecure",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{shortToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Data exposure: search",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Expected: a search result never contains password data",
                  "pm.test('API3 Data exposure: no password data in search results', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.match(/password/i);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insecure/search?q=t",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "insecure",
                "search"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "t"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Verbose error: a quote in the search",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Expected: odd input gets a normal answer, never HOW the server works",
                  "pm.test('API8 Verbose error: no SQL or stack trace in the answer', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'status').to.be.below(500);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.match(/SELECT|stack|Exception/i);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insecure/search?q='",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "insecure",
                "search"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "'"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
